<node name="CWPE Prep Notes" unique_id="1" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="#f05517" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h1" weight="heavy" foreground="#f05517">CWPE Prep Notes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Certified Wi-Fi Pentesting Expert. This file holds your methodology, module notes and exam workspace as a tree of nodes. Pick a node on the left to open it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#f05517">The exam
</rich_text>
<rich_text>CWPE is a 7-day wireless exam in HTB's cloud lab, so you don't need your own hardware. You attack a real-world wireless setup: WEP, WPA, WPA2 and WPA3 networks, captive portals, and a corporate Wi-Fi network that leads into Active Directory. Flags prove each step, and you finish with a commercial-grade report.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Four parts:</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 2" foreground="#f05517">Methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your methodology, as numbered blank phases that you name and fill in your own way.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 13" foreground="#f05517">Modules</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your notes, one per Academy module, in course order. Your methodology links back to these.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 197" foreground="#f05517">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your exam workspace, with networks and hosts, credentials, findings, flags and a log for each day, laid out like the report.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="webs https://cnmoseman.github.io/htb-study-trackers/cwpe/tracker/" foreground="#f05517">CWPE Study Tracker</rich_text>
<rich_text>: the day-by-day study plan for this cert. Check off tasks there as you go.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#d9822b">Read this first
</rich_text>
<rich_text>CWPE launched in 2026 and nobody has published an exam write-up yet. Lean on the last module, Attacking Corporate Wi-Fi Networks, which runs a full engagement end to end, and practice the report before you book.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#2f9e44">Do the reporting module
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Do the </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://academy.hackthebox.com/course/preview/documentation--reporting" foreground="#f05517">Documentation &amp; Reporting</rich_text>
<rich_text> module from the Penetration Tester path before your exam, even though it isn't in the CWPE path. It shows you how to take notes during an engagement and turn them into the kind of report HTB grades. It's built around the CPTS report, so it won't match the CWPE report one for one. Take the general tips and good habits from it and apply them to the CWPE report template.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#f05517">How to use it</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>1. Work through the course in order. As you finish each module, fill in its note.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>2. Build your methodology as you go. Rename each </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#f05517">Fill in</rich_text>
<rich_text> phase to a step in your own workflow, and add or delete phases as you need. For a new phase, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Methodology Phase</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>3. Fill each phase with your own checklist, commands and decision points, and link back to the module notes: select some text, pick </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Insert › Insert/Edit Link</rich_text>
<rich_text>, choose </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">To Node</rich_text>
<rich_text> and pick the note.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>4. Keep one node per tool and one per protocol under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tools &amp; Protocols</rich_text>
<rich_text>. For a new one, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Tool</rich_text>
<rich_text> or </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Protocol</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tools &amp; Protocols</rich_text>
<rich_text>. </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 195" foreground="#f05517">Aircrack-ng</rich_text>
<rich_text> and </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 196" foreground="#f05517">WPS</rich_text>
<rich_text> are there to start you off. Link them from your module notes and phases so the commands you use most are one click away.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>5. Each module has one child node per Academy section. Expand a module in the tree to see its sections.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>6. On exam day, start at </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 197" foreground="#f05517">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> and work from your methodology. The main nodes are in the </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Bookmarks</rich_text>
<rich_text> menu. Click any link to jump to the node behind it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#f05517">Command sources</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Get tested commands from these as you go:</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://github.com/V0lk3n/WirelessPentesting-CheatSheet" foreground="#f05517">V0lk3n wireless cheat sheet</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://github.com/armourinfosec/Wireless-Security-and-WiFi-Penetration-Testing" foreground="#f05517">armourinfosec wireless cheat sheet</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://hacktricks.wiki/en/generic-methodologies-and-resources/pentesting-wifi/index.html" foreground="#f05517">HackTricks Wi-Fi methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>Reporting: </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://docs.sysreptor.com/assets/reports/HTB-CWPE-Report.pdf" foreground="#f05517">SysReptor HTB-CWPE template</rich_text>
<rich_text> + </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://academy.hackthebox.com/course/preview/documentation--reporting" foreground="#f05517">Documentation &amp; Reporting module</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">Made by</rich_text>
<rich_text> </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://github.com/cnmoseman" foreground="#f05517">cnmoseman</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
